skill: Excel

@ Formulas and Functions | B
Which function adds the numbers in a range of cells?
= SUM
- ADD
- TOTAL
- PLUS
? =SUM(A1:A10) adds all numbers in the range.

@ Formulas and Functions | B
Which character must every Excel formula start with?
= =
- #
- @
- $
? Typing an equals sign tells Excel that the cell contains a formula.

@ Formulas and Functions | I
What does =COUNTIF(A1:A10, ">50") return?
= The number of cells in A1:A10 that are greater than 50
- The sum of values greater than 50
- The average of values greater than 50
- An error
? COUNTIF counts cells that meet a single condition.

@ Formulas and Functions | I
What does the $ sign do in the reference $A$1?
= Makes the reference absolute so it does not change when the formula is copied
- Formats the cell as currency
- Locks the worksheet
- Converts the value to text
? $A$1 keeps both the column and the row fixed. $A1 fixes only the column.

@ Formulas and Functions | I
What does =IFERROR(A1/B1, 0) do?
= Returns 0 when the division produces an error
- Always returns 0
- Highlights errors in red
- Deletes the cell when B1 is empty
? IFERROR returns the second argument if the first one evaluates to an error such as #DIV/0!.

@ Formulas and Functions | I
Which function returns the number of non-empty cells in a range?
= COUNTA
- COUNT
- COUNTBLANK
- LEN
? COUNT counts only numeric cells. COUNTA counts every cell that is not empty.

@ Lookup Functions | I
Which function searches the first column of a table and returns a value from another column in the same row?
= VLOOKUP
- HLOOKUP
- SUMIF
- COUNTA
? VLOOKUP looks down the first column. HLOOKUP searches across the first row.

@ Lookup Functions | I
In =VLOOKUP(A2, D:F, 3, FALSE), what does FALSE mean?
= Look for an exact match
- Return the result as text
- Sort the table first
- Ignore blank cells
? The last argument FALSE (or 0) requests an exact match. TRUE allows an approximate match on sorted data.

@ Lookup Functions | A
Which function is often combined with MATCH as a more flexible alternative to VLOOKUP?
= INDEX
- CHOOSE
- ROUND
- TRIM
? INDEX returns the value at a position and MATCH finds that position, so you can look up in any direction.

@ Data Cleaning in Excel | I
Which function removes extra spaces from text, including leading, trailing and repeated spaces?
= TRIM
- CLEAN
- LEN
- FIND
? TRIM leaves single spaces between words. CLEAN removes non-printable characters.

@ Data Cleaning in Excel | I
Which Excel feature quickly removes duplicate rows from a data range?
= Data > Remove Duplicates
- Conditional Formatting
- Freeze Panes
- Goal Seek
? Remove Duplicates keeps the first row for each unique combination of the selected columns.

@ Data Cleaning in Excel | I
Which function joins text from several cells using a delimiter?
= TEXTJOIN
- LEN
- FIND
- TRIMMEAN
? TEXTJOIN(delimiter, ignore_empty, range) combines text with a separator.

@ PivotTables | B
What is a PivotTable used for?
= Summarizing and analyzing large data sets interactively
- Checking spelling in a sheet
- Writing macros
- Formatting fonts
? PivotTables let you group, filter and aggregate data without writing formulas.

@ Charts | B
Which chart type is best for showing how a value changes over time?
= Line chart
- Pie chart
- Radar chart
- Bubble chart
? Line charts connect data points in time order, which makes trends easy to see.
